# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots Cassandra (backgrounded, as the cassandra user) with
# the vulnerable AllowAllAuthenticator + UDF config, then execs `sleep infinity`,
# so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING with unauthenticated access when the agent
#     starts, which makes the "edited cassandra.yaml but never restarted" case
#     detectable (the live node still accepts unauthenticated CQL);
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting Cassandra cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must switch to PasswordAuthenticator,
# disable UDFs, AND RESTART Cassandra so the new authenticator takes effect.
# Cassandra boots slowly (~60-90s); wait for readiness after restart.
